ailway stations; \n \n(b) if so, the time by which all the said trains are likely to be \nresumed; \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(d) whether the Government is considering to stop Samta Express, \nPuri-Ahmedabad Express, Korba -Vishakhapatnam train and \nTirupati-Bilaspur train at Nuapada Railway Station; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (c) To provide better passenger safety by creating \nmaintenance corridor blocks, minimizing conflicts in existing time \ntable etc., Indian Railways  had undertaken rationalization of time \n\ntable (including that of stoppages) in a scientific manner with the \nassistance of IIT -Bombay. Since November -2021, Mail/Express \nservices are being operated as per rationalized time table and \nstoppages. To cater to th e needs of passengers of Norla Road and \nRupra Road, stoppage of 3 pairs of trains at Norla Road station and \n2 pairs of trains at Rupra Road have been provided w.e.f. \n14.05.2022.  Further, at present, Lanjigarh Road station is being \nadequately served by 05 pairs of train services. Besides, provision \nof stoppages is an on -going process on Indian Railways subject to \noperational feasibility and commercial justification etc. \n \n(d) & (e) Stoppages of 12843/44 Puri -Ahmedabad Express, \n18517/18 Korba -Viskhapatnam Express & 17481/82 Bilaspur -\nTirupati Express have been provided at Nawapara Road w.e.f. \n23.08.2022.  \n***** \n�\n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |105", "t": "Introduction of Trains between Tirupati and Shirdi", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 105 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2022 \n \nINTRODUCTION OF TRAINS BETWEEN TIRUPATI AND SHIRDI \n \n*105. SHRI MADDILA GURUMOORTHY: \n      \n         Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether progress has been 