 details of the amount spent annually by the Indian  railways on \nthe maintenance of electric  and diesel locomotives separately; \n(d)  whether it is possible to develop and operate such locomotives \nwhich can use ethanol or bio-diesel; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof ?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a)  to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n---2/- \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 107 BY SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH JOSHI  AND SHRI \nRODMAL NAGAR  TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 14.12.2022 \nREGARDING ANNUAL BILL FOR IMPORTED FUEL \n \n(a)   the year wise details of amount (including Freight and other taxes  \netc.) spent by Indian Railways on high speed diesel; \n \nYear Amount spent in Crores of  \n2018-19 18587.14  \n2019-20 16377.60 \n2020-21 11438.70 \n \n(b)  There has been no direct import of HSD (High-speed diesel) by Indian  \nRailways. \n   \n(c) The amount spent annually by the Indian R ailways on the maintenance \nof electric and diesel locomotives for three years is as under: \n \nYear Amount in Crores of  \nElectric Diesel \n2018-19 2262.90 3669.48 \n2019-20 2430.76 3508.27 \n2020-21 2344.86 2687.28 \n   \n(d) &  (e) Yes, Sir. It is possible to operate locomotives on ethanol/bio -     \ndiesel after blending with other fuels. Operation of diesel locomotives \nwith B-5 Bio-diesel have been tested by Research Designs and Standards \nOrganisation (RDSO). \n \n***** \n \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |108", "t": "Government Services available on Digital Platform", "head": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \n DEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 108  \nFOR ANSWER ON 14TH DECEMBER, 2022  \n  \nGOVERNMENT SERVICES AVAILABLE ON DIGITAL PLATFORM \n \n*108.  SHRI KULDEEP RAI SHARMA: \nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n \nWill 