������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |196", "t": "Mandatory Apps based Attendance under MGNREGS", "head": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 196 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n \n5G SERVICES BY BSNL/MTNL \n \n†196.  SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH:  \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether it is a fact that Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL) has made any demand with the \nGovernment to reserve 70MHz airwaves of 5G spectrum for its 5G;  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  whether BSNL and MTNL have taken any steps and started trials to launch 5G services in the \ncountry;  \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(e)  whether the Government has signed any agreement with Indian and foreign companies for 5G \nservices; and  \n \n(f)  if so, the details thereof?   \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR COMMUNICATIONS \n(SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN) \n \n(a) & (b)  As part of the Cabinet decision on the conduct of Spectrum Auctions held in July \n2022, 10 MHz of paired spectrum in the 600 MHz band, 40 MHz in the 3300 MHz band and 400 \nMHz in the 26 GHz band has been reserved in all Licence Service Areas for providing 5G \nservices by BSNL. Further BSNL has  also requested for reservation of 10 MHz of paired \nspectrum in the 700 MHz in lieu of the already reserved 10 MHz in the 600 MHz band, and \nadditional 30 MHz and 400 MHz of spectrum in the 3300 MHz band and 26 GHz band \nrespectively in all Licence Service Areas (LSAs). \n(c) & (d)  5G Non Standalone Access (NSA) upgrade has been kept as a deferred feature in \nBSNL’s EOI (Expression of Interest) dated 01.01.2021 for Registration -cum- Participation and \nProof of Concept for 4G tender of BSNL. As per EOI condition, BSNL has asked M/s Tata \nConsultancy Services (TCS) to offer the equipment for 5G NSA testing (deferred feature) so as \nto enable BSNL to start the trial for 5G services. \n(e) & (f)  The Government has not signed any agreement with Indian and foreign \ncompanies for 5G services. \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |197", "t": "Acreage under Rapeseed", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n197\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n2\n0\nTH\nDECEMBER\n,\n \n202\n2\n \n \nACREAGE UNDER RAPESEED\n \n \n*\n197\n.\n \n  \nSHRI RAHUL RAMESH SHEWALE:\n \n  \nDR. PRITAM \nGOPINA\nTHRAO MUNDE:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \nिकसान\n \nक\u0000ाण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether \nthe \nfarmers have increased acreage under rapeseed as compared to the \nlast year season;\n \n(b)\n \nif so, the \ndetails\n \nthereof;\n \n(c)\n \nwhether the higher oilseed output will help the country to cut expensive purchases\n \nof edible oils from Malaysia, Indonesia, Brazil, Argentina, Russia and Ukrain\ne\n; and\n \n(d)\n \nif so, the steps taken or proposed to be taken by the Government to encourage the \nfarmers to increase the acreage under rapeseed cultivation? \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICUL\nTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \nिकसान\n \nक\u0000ाण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n   \n(SHRI NAREDNRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (d): \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n\nSTATEMENT IN RESPECT OF PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 197\n \nDUE FOR\n \nANSWER ON 20.12.2022 REGARDING ACREAGE UND\nER \nR\nAPESEED\n.\n \n \n(a) \nto \n(\nd\n)\n:\n \n \nThe Government has been implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme viz., \nNational Food Security Mission\n-\n \nOilseeds & Oil palm (NFSM\n-\nOS&OP) from 2018\n-\n19 to augment \nthe availability of edible oils by increasing the production and pro\nductivi\nty of nine oilseed crops \ninc\nluding Rapeseed & \nMustard (R&M) and to reducing the import burden in the country. \nFrom the \nyear 2021, the Government is implementing the National Mission on Edible Oils\n-\n \nOil Palm for \nincreasing edible oil production and r\neducing\n \nimport dependency. \n \n \nUnder the NFSM\n-\n \nOilseeds, incentives/ subsidies are being provided to the farmers \nthrough State Government for three broad interventions viz. (i) seed component covering \npurchase of breeder seeds , production of foundation seed\ns & cer\ntified seeds, distribution of \ncertified seeds, distribution of seed minikits & seed hub (ii) production inputs component covering \nseed infrastructure development, seed storage bins, Plant Protection (PP) equipments & seed \ntreating drum, PP chemicals\n, distr\nibution of gypsum/ pyrites/ lime etc., Nuclear Polyhedrosis \nVirus/ bio agent, supply of bio\n-\nfertilizers, improved farm implements, sprinkler sets, water \ncarrying pipes, and (iii) transfer of technology component covering cluster/ block demonstration\ns, \nFron\ntline Demonstrations, Cluster Frontline Demonstrations and training through National \nAgricultural Research System and Krishi Vigyan Kendra, Integrated Pest Management through \nFarmer Field School (FFS) mode, training of farmers, training of officers/\n \nextens\nion workers, \nneed based R&D project including seminar/ kisan mela and oil extraction unit under flexi funds \netc. \n \n \nT\nhe acreage under rapeseed & mustard has increased from 67.00 lakh hectare in 2020\n-\n21 to 80.59 lakh hectare during the year 2021\n-\n22 (4\nth\n \nAdva\nnce Estimate, Directorate of \nEconomics & Statistics). \nMoreover, t\nhe\n \ntotal \narea, production and \nproductivity of \noilseeds in the \ncountry \nhas \nalso increased\n, details \nof which \nare given below: \n \n \nY\near\n \nArea\n \n(L\nakh hectare)\n \nProduction\n \n(L\nakh tones)\n \nProductiv\nity\n \n(Kg\n./ hectare)\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n247.94\n \n315.22\n \n1271\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n271.39\n \n332.19\n \n1224\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n288.34\n \n359.46\n \n1247\n \n2021\n-\n22*\n \n291.67\n \n376.96\n \n1292\n \n* 4\nth\n \nAdvance Estimate, Directorate of Economics & Statistics\n.\n \n\n \nThough t\nh\ne domestic availability of edible oils has increa\nsed from \n10\n3\n.5\n2\n \nlakh tonnes in \n201\n8\n-\n19\n \nto 115.71 lakh tonnes in 2021\n-\n22,\n \ndue to higher \ndemand\n \nof \nedible oil\n,\n \nthe deficit is being \nmet through imports.\n \nHowever, if the domestic availability had not increased, it would have led to \neven higher imports. \n \n \nUnder NFSM\n-\nOS\n, \nin the year 2021\n-\n22\n, \n5.98 lakh mini kits were distributed free to the \nfarmers. In the year 2022\n-\n23, 5.75 lakh min kits have been allotted for distribution during Rabi \n2022\n-\n23. The mini kits are of 2 kg size consisting of seeds of high yieldi\nng varieties \nhaving \nproductivity more than 20 quintals per hectare.\n \n \nIn\n \nthe year 2021\n-\n22\n,\n \n11.86 lakh mini kits were distributed free of cost to farmers in \nhigh \npotential districts\n \nof 9 states. In the year 2022\n-\n23, 26.50 lakh mini kits have been allocated f\nor \nhigh poten\ntial districts of 18 states.\n \n \nMoreover, the Government has distributed 1.20 lakh mini kits of hybrid seeds during \n2021\n-\n22 in 5 \ns\ntates.\n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |198", "t": "Projected Employment under MGNREGS", "head": " \n  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 198 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/12/2022 \n \nPROJECTED EMPLOYMENT UNDER MGNREGS \n \n*198.  DR. A. CHELLAKUMAR: \nADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \n \n  Will the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware that Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment \nGuarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) is projected to employ people from over 70 million \nfamilies in Financial Year 2022-2023 indicating that overall economic growth which is \nstill not reaching the rural and unorganised sections of the country; \n(b)  whether the Government is aware that as compared to the corresponding pre-COVID \nmonth of October 2019, about 15.5 million households applied for jobs through the \nMGNREGS in October 2022; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n(d)  whether the Government is aware that in contrast to its two lakh target, the Unnati \ninitiative, which was launched in 2020 to reduce reliance on the MGNREGS, has trained \nonly 25,056 people; and \n(e)  if so, the reasons therefor along with the steps taken by the Government to address the \nissue? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n   \n \n(a) to (e):       A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n \n \nStatement in reply to Parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 198 for 20.12.2022 \n  \n(a)to(c):   Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGS) is a demand driven wage employment Scheme which provides for the enhancement of \nlivelihood security of the households in rural areas of the country by providing at  least one \nhundred days of guaranteed wage employment in every financial year to every household whose \nadult members volunteer to do unskilled manual work.  \n  \nIn current financial year 2022 -23 (as on 15.12.2022), a total of 538.04 lakh households \nhave availed employment under Mahatma Gandhi NREGS. \n  \nDetails of the households demanded employment in the month of October, 2019 and \nOctober, 2022 is given below: \n  \nPeriod October, 2019 October, 2022 \nHouseholds demanded employment (in lakh) 129.18 155.45 \n  \nIt provides livelihood security, i.e. fall back options for livelihood for the rural \nhouseholds, when no better employment opportunity is available.  \n  \n(d) & (e): The Government of India has launched “Project UNNATI” in December 2019 \nwhich intends to upgrade the skill -base of the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment \nGuarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi NREGS) workers, and thereby improve their \nlivelihoods, so that they can move from the current partial employment to full employment \nthrough either self employment or wage employment. The Project aims to enhance the skill \nbase of 2 lakh Mahatma Gandhi NREGS beneficiaries. \n  \nThe slow pace of implementation of the “Project UNNATI” at the State level is being \nregularly reviewed by the Ministry with the State Rural Livelihood Missions of the concerned \nStates. The issue, if any, comes to the notice of this Ministry is addressed immediately. So far, \n27,383 (as on 30.11.2022) candidates have been trained. \n \n \n*******  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |199", "t": "Effects of Climate Change on Crops", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 199 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \nANGAMALY SABARI RAILWAY PROJECT \n \n199. SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n SHRI KODIKUNNIL SURESH: \n ADV. DEAN KURIAKOSE: \n SHRI BENNY BEHANAN:  \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the present status of works, implementation and stage of approval of Angamaly -\nSabarimala railway project of Southern Railway; \n \n(b) whether the Government is intending to fully allocate necessary funds for the \ncompletion of the project or proposes a cost sharing model between Government \nof Kerala and Ministry of Railways, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has received a revised project proposal after the final \nlocation survey from the Government of Kerala, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government of Kerala can restart the land acquisition in the Social \nImpact Assessment study completed areas of this project, if so, the details \nthereof; \n \n(e) whether the Hon’ble Prime Minister has inclu ded this project in PRAGATI Scheme \non 26th October, 2016; \n \n(f) if so, whether the said railway line is likely to have the necessary infrastructure to \nrun the Vande Bharat Express trains; \n \n(g) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(h) whether the Railways plans to expand t he project from Azutha to \nThiruvananthapuram via Pathanamthitta and Punalur thereby connecting it with \nKollam-Shenkotta railway line, which will provide railway connectivity from Tamil \nNadu to Sabarimala, if so, the details in this regard?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (h): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (h) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 199 BY SHRI ANTO ANTONY, SHRI \nKODIKUNNIL SURESH, ADV. DEAN KURIAKOSE AND SHRI BENNY \nBEHANAN TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 07.12.2022  REGARDING \nANGAMALY SABARI RAILWAY PROJECT \n \n(a) to (d):  Angamali-Sabarimala new line (116 Km) was sanctioned in \n1997-98 at a cost of ` 550 crore. Work on Angamali-Kaladi (7 Km) and long \nlead works on Kaladi -Perumbavoor (10 Km) have been taken up. However, \nfurther works on this project could not be taken forward due to protests \nby local people against land acquisition and fixing of alignment of the line, \ncourt cases filed against the project and inadequate support from the \nState Government of Kerala.  \n \n After long persuasion, Government of Kerala vide letter dated \n07.01.2021 has conveyed their decision to share 50% of the total project \ncost ( ` 2815 crore) of Angamali - Sabarimala Railway project through \nKerala Infrastructure Investment Fund Board (KIIFB), subject to the \ncondition that operation and maintenance of the track shall be done by \nMinistry of Railways while the stations along th e route  will be developed \nby a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) (through public private partnership \nroute) and the net revenue realized by the SPV will be shared on a 50:50 \nbasis between State Government and Ministry of Railways, after offsetting \nthe cost of Operation & Maintenance (O&M) as agreed to by Railways. M/s \nKerala Rail Development Corporation Limited (KRDCL ) has been advised \non 20.07.2021 to complete Final Location Survey and to update the \nproject cost.     \n …2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \n \n Accordingly, M/s KRDCL completed the Final Location Survey (FLS) \nand has prepared the Detailed Estimate (DE) of the full project.  \n \n(e) to (g) : Angamali-Erumeli new Railway line project has already been \nincluded in PRAGATI projects. All newly sanctioned projects are designed \nwith track infrastructure capable to run all existing trains of Indian \nRailway network including Vande Bharat Express train. \n \n(h):  Survey for a new line between Erumeli and Thiruvananthapuram via \nPathanamthitta and Punalur was completed in 2013. The project could not \nbe taken forward due to low traffic projections as per survey reports. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |2", "t": "Auction of Coal Blocks", "head": "�\n������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n����������������������� � �\n������������������ ���������� �\n�\n���������������� ������ ������������������� �\n�\n��� �������������������� ���\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� �� ���� ������� ��� ���� ���� ������ ������� �������� ����� ��������� ����\n������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� �� ����� ������ ����� ��� ����� ������������ ���������� ����� ����� ���� ������\n����������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� �� ���� ������ ������� ��� ������������� �� ��� ���� ����� ����� ���� ����\n������������������������������������������� �\n�\n������ �\n�\n���������������������������������������� �\n������������������������������������ �\n�\n����������������������� �\n�\n������������ ���������������������������������������������� �\n����� �\n� �\n\n�\n��������� � ��������� ��� ��� ������ ���