�������� ������������ ��� ���������������� ���������� ������� ������\n���������������� ��� �������� ���� ���������� ���� �������� ����� ��� ����� ����� ��� �������� ����� ����\n����������� ����� ������ ��� ������� ��� ������� ����� ���������������������� �������� ������������\n�������������������� ��� �������������� ����� ������� ��������� ���������������� ����������\n��������� ������������������������ ��������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� �������� ���� ��� ��� ���������� ��� ���� ������������� ������� ���������������������������\n�������� ��� ���������������� ���������� ���������������� ��� ���� ����� ��� ���� ��������������� ���\n����� ����������� ���������� �������������� �������� ��� ����������� ��� ������ ��������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ ������ ��� ������� �������� ���� ��������� ��� ��� ���������� ������ ��� ��������������� ��� �����\n������������\n�\n��������\n�\n� �\n\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |73", "t": "AMU Malappuram Centre", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 73 \nANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 \n \nAMU MALAPPURAM CENTRE \n \n*73. SHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it has come to the notice of the Government that as per Advertisement No. 03/2019 \ndated 25/10/2019 and Advertisement No. 02/2022(T) dated 31.05.2022 a lot of vacancies continue \nto exist in AM U Malappuram Centre for a long time since 2019 for non -Teaching posts of Private \nSecretary and teaching posts like Professors to Research Assistants; \n(b) if so, whether the Government has taken note that the process of recruitment is yet to take place \nand these posts are still vacant; \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor and the time by which these vacancies are \nlikely to be filled; \n(d) whether sufficient funds have not been released to Malappuram Centre of AMU; \n(e) if so, the details of yearly requirements and allocation of funds to this Centre from 2019 to the \ncurrent year; and \n(f) the time by which sufficient funds are likely to be released and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF EDUCATION \n \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n \n(a)  to (f) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.73 TO BE ANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 REGARDING “AMU \nMALAPPURAM CENTRE” ASKED BY SHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN, HON’BLE \nMEMBER OF PARLIAMENT. \n \n(a) to (c) Central Universities are autono mous bodies, established under respective Central Acts. \nThe teachers in Universities and Colleges are recruited as per Acts, Statutes, Ordinances, etc. of the \nrespective Universities. Besides this, there are guidelines issued by the University Grants \nCommission (UGC) for appointment of teachers and other academic staff in Universities and \nColleges. As per information provided from AMU, vide advertisement no. 03/2019 (NT) dated \n25/10/2019, one post of Private Secretary was advertised and vide advertisement no. 02/2022(T) \ndated 31.05.2022, 2 posts of Assistant Professors were advertised for AMU Malappuram Centre.  \n (d) to (f) Funds are released to the University by UGC , enblock, for the main campus and centres \ntogether. University assesses the requirement based on demand proje cted by the Center and \nthereafter releases funds to these centres. The details of funds released to AMU Malappuram Centre \nfrom 2019 are as below: \n                                  \n           (Rs. In Crore) \nYear Budget Allocated/ Released \n \n2019-20 \n \n2.40 \n2020-21 \n \n2.40 \n2021-22 \n \n2.53 \n2022-23 \n \n4.23 \n \n     **** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |75", "t": "Reservation for STs in Telangana", "head": " \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 75 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2022 \n \n \n \nSTART-UP COMPANIES \n \n \n \n75. SHRI ANIL FIROJIYA:  \n      SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA: \n \n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n \n(a) the mannner in which Indian apparel and Indian artisans are being promoted to make the textiles sector of \nour country popular in the global market; and  \n \n(b) the steps being taken to promote start -up companies and young scientists in specialised sectors like \ntechnical apparel? \n \n \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्‍ य मंत्री (श्रीमती दर्शना जरदोर्) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES  \n (SMT. DARSHANA JARDOSH) \n \n(a):  To promote Indian apparel and Indian artisans of textiles sector in the global market, Government is \nimplementing various schemes/ programmes such as Production Linked Incentive Scheme , Pradhan Mantri \nMega Integrated Textile Region and Apparel , National Technical Textiles Mission , Scheme for Integrated \nTextile Parks,  SAMARTH- Scheme for Capacity Building in Textile Sector, Silk Samagra 2.0, National \nHandloom Development Programme, Raw Material Supply Scheme, National Handicraft Development \nProgramme, Comprehensive Handicrafts Cluster Development Scheme, Integrated Wool Development \nProgramme etc. \n \n(b): In order to encourage indigenous research and developmental activities in the field of technical \ntextiles including technical apparel, National Technical Textiles Mission is being implemented with \nbudgetary outlay of Rs. 1,480 cr.    \n*** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |76", "t": "NSSO 68th Round Data", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *76 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 \n \nNSSO 68TH ROUND DATA \n \n*76.  SHRI N. REDDEPPA: \n \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPR ENEURSHIP be \npleased to state : \n \n(a)   whether the Government is aware that as per C ensus 2011 and National Sample Survey \nOffice (NSSO) 68th Round data, around 104 million f resh entrants to the workforce will require \nskill training by 2022; \n \n(b)   if so, the steps taken to encourage outcome b ased skill development training among the \nmasses; \n \n(c)    whether the Skill India Programme is on trac k to meet intended targets by 2022; and  \n \n(d)   if so, the details thereof and if not, the re asons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OFSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (D) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *76 TO BE ANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 ASKED  BY SHRI N. REDDEPPA  \nREGARDING “NSSO 68TH ROUND DATA”.  \n \n(a) Vision of National Policy for Skill Development  & Entrepreneurship (NPSDE), 2015 is to \ncreate an ecosystem of empowerment by Skilling on a  large Scale at Speed with high \nStandards and to promote a culture of innovation ba sed entrepreneurship which can generate \nwealth and employment so as to ensure Sustainable l ivelihoods for all citizens in the country. \nWith a view to guide the policy intervention to rea lize this vision, estimate of skilling requirement \nhas been provided in the policy document, as per wh ich the fresh entrants between 2015-22 \nrequiring skilling/ Vocational Education Training ( VET) is 104.62 million. This estimate is based \non 66 \nth  and 68 th  round of National Sample Survey Organisation (NSSO ) and Census, 2011 \ndata. \n \n(b) In order to meet skilling requirement for futur e workforce, improve the quality of skilling \nand align the training programs with the changes in  the economy and technology to meet the \nneeds of the industry, following steps have been ta ken by Ministry of Skill Development and \nEntrepreneurship (MSDE): \n \n(i)   Expansion in infrastructure of Industrial Tra ining Institutes (ITIs) through new ITIs \nin Public and Private Sectors. \n \n(ii)   Upgradation and modernization of ITIs in ter ms of their infrastructure, pedagogy, \ncurriculum and technology interventions. \n \n(iii)   Introduction of new-age courses in Internet  of Things (IoT), Renewable Energy, \nAdditive Manufacturing Technology (3-D Printing), Mechatronics, Drone Technology in ITIs. \n(iv) Launching of the Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY), for imparting short-\nterm skill training to the youth. \n \n(v)   Implementation of JSS to impart Vocational Sk ills to non-literates, neo-literates \nand the persons having rudimentary level of educati on upto  8 th  standard and school \ndropouts upto 12th standard in the age group of 15-45 years. \n \n(vi)   Notification of common norms for bringing ab out uniformity and standardization in \nimplementation of various Skill Development schemes by different Central  Ministries/ \nDepartments.  \n \n(vii) Setting up of Sector Skill Councils (SSCs) as  industry-led bodies to develop \nNational Occupation Standards (NOSs). \n \n(viii) Implementation of Skills Acquisition and Kno wledge Awareness for Livelihood \nPromotion (SANKALP), an outcome-oriented World Bank  supported project for \nstrengthening institutional mechanisms at both national and state levels.  \n \n(ix)   Implementation of Skills Strengthening for I ndustrial Value Enhancement \n(STRIVE) scheme, a World Bank assisted project laun ched with the objective of improving \nthe relevance and efficiency of skills training pro vided through Industrial Training Institutes \n(ITIs) and apprenticeships.  \n \n(x)   Mobilisation/ Soutreach activities through Ka ushal/ Rozgar Melas, Skills Career \nCounselling Scheme in making skilling aspirational. \n \n(xi)   Alignment of courses as per National Skill Q ualification Framework (NSQF). \n \n\n(xii) Trainings of Trainers through National Skill Training Institutes (NSTIs) and \nInstitutes of Training of Trainers (IToTs). \n \n(c) and (d) Details of number of persons trained un der various schemes of MSDE is as \nfollows: \n \nScheme  under MSDE  Number of persons  trained  (in Lakh)  \nPMKVY (since 2015 upto September, 2022 137.17 \nJSS (from 2018-19 to September, 2022) 14.65 \nNAPS (from 2018-19 to September, 2022) 16.74 \nCTS (from 2014 to September, 2022) 98.84 \n \nIn addition, 188.44 Lakh persons were provided fee- based training by NSDC till October, \n2022. A total of 13.12 Lakh persons have been train ed under Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – \nNational Urban Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NULM) of Mi nistry of Housing and Urban Affairs \n(MoHUA) and 12.94 Lakh persons have been trained un der Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) and 33.66 Lakh persons h ave been trained under Ru"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |77", "t": "Development of Iconic Sites in Karnataka", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*77  \nANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF ICONIC SITES IN KARNATAKA \n*77. SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR: \n      Will the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has initiated action to prepare a \ncomprehensive master plan for the development of Iconic Sites \nlocated in Karnataka with special budgetary allocation to serve \nas models; \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the major items of work to be \nexecuted on these sites; and \n(c)  whether other sites would be identified for development as \nIconic Sites in future and if so, the details thereof? \n  \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM      (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *77 ANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 REGARDING \nDEVELOPMENT OF ICONIC SITES IN KARNATKAKA. \n \n(a) to (c): The Ministry of Tourism had formulated ‘Development of \nIconic Tourist Destination s Scheme’ for development of identified \niconic destinations in the country including Hampi in Karnataka \nfollowing a holistic approach. A master plan for Hampi was prepared \nby the Ministry.  However, the scheme is not approved.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |78", "t": "Vacant Teaching Posts in Universities/HEIs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION No.78 \nANSWERED ON 12.12.2022 \n \nVACANT TEACHING POSTS IN UNIVERSITIES/HEIs \n \n*78. ADV. A.M. ARIFF:  \n       SHRI RAVIKUMAR D.: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken note that over 33 per cent of the sanctioned teaching posts \nare vacant in central universities across the country seriously affecting the quality of education; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) the steps taken/likely to be taken by the Government to fill the vacancies of teaching faculty \nin various Higher Education Institutions HEIs in the country including the backlog vacancies \nmeant for Scheduled Castes (SCs) in teaching posts in a time bound manner; and \n(d) the details of number of sanctioned positions and vacant positions in various Higher \nEducation Institutions including Indian Institute of Technology (IITs), Indian Institute of \nManagement (IIMs), and Central Universities, institution -wise and post -wise, reserved and \nunreserved separately? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 78 FOR ANSWER ON 12TH DECEMBER, 2022 ASKED BY \nADV. A.M. ARIFF AND SHRI RAVIKUMAR D. , HON’BLE MEMBERS  OF \nPARLIAMENT REGARDING VACANT TEACHING POSTS IN UNIVERSITIES/HEIs. \n \n(a) & (b) Occurrence of vacancies and filling thereof is a continuous process. Central Universities \nare autonomous bodies, established under respective Central Acts. They are governed by \nprovisions of the Acts/Statues/Ordinances made thereunder. Their recruitment procedure is \nformulated by their statutory b odies in accordance with their Acts/Statues/Rules and UGC \nregulations/guidelines. Out of 18956 sanctioned teaching posts in 45 Central Universities  in \nregular mode under the purview of Ministry of Education, 12776 posts are filled up and 6180 \nposts are vacant as on 01.12.2022. Ministry of Education has also directed all Higher Education \nInstitutions (HEIs) to fill up the vacancies in a Mission Mode. \n(c) In addition to writing to all the HEIs to fill up the vacancies in a Mission Mode , the Ministry \nhas set up a monthly monitoring mechanism. The Central Educational Institutions (Reservation in \nTeachers Cadre) Act, 2019 has been notified on 09.07.2019 to ensure preparation of the rosters \nby considering the university as a Unit. Also, according to the Act, reservation is applicable in all \nthe Higher E ducational Institutions except the institutions listed in the schedule and few other \nexceptions as stated in the Act. Further, as per this Act, reservation is provided for all posts in \ndirect recruitment in Teacher’s  cadre in Central Educational Institutions.  After enactment of this \nAct, no reserved post is to be de-reserved. \n(d) Institutions-wise and post-wise details of number of sanctioned positions and vacant positions \nin various Higher Education Institutions incl uding Indian Institute of Technology (IITs), Indian  \nInstitute of Management (IIMs) and Central Universities are annexed. \n \n***** \n\nAnnexure \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.78 FOR ANSWER ON 12.12.2022 \nASKED BY ADV.  A.M. ARIFF AND SHRI RAVIKUMAR D., HON’BLE MEMBERS OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING VACANT \nTEACHING POSTS IN UNIVERSITIES/ HEIs. \nSl. \nNo. Institutions Posts \nNo. of sanctioned posts  No of Vacant Posts \nGEN SC ST OBC EWS PWD TOTAL GEN SC ST OBC EWS PWD TOTAL \n1 \nCentral \nUniversities \n(CUs) \nProfessor 1564 307 142 367 111 62 2553 705 231 124 311 101 57 1529 \nAssociate \nProfessor 3073 620 302 752 233 130 5110 771 401 232 576 211 113 2304 \nAssistant \nProfessor 6099 1357 698 2332 486 321 11293 791 276 188 672 289 131 2347 \n2 \nIndian \nInstitute of \nTechnology \n(IITs)* \nFaculty \nPosts 11170 4502 \n3 \nIndian \nInstitute of \nManagement \n(IIMs)* \nFaculty \nPosts 1197 97 40 184 48 \nNo \nseparate \ncategory \n1566 266 53 34 98 42 \nNo \nseparate \ncategory \n493 \n \n*IITs and IIMs follow flexi cadre for faculty posts. \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |79", "t": "Inclusion of Nomadic Tribes in the List of STs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO- *79 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 12/12/2022 \n  \nINCLUSION OF NOMADIC TRIBES IN THE LIST OF STs \n  \n*79.    SHRI T.R. BAALU: \n            \nWill the Minister of TRIBAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether it is a fact that many nomadic tribes living in plains of various States like \nNarikuravar in Tamil Nadu are not categorized as Scheduled Tribes (STs) despite their \neducational, social, and economic status being very low than many of the Scheduled Tribes; \n(b) whether any representation has been received by the Union Government demanding the \ninclusion of such tribal communities in the list of STs; \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Government in this regard; and \n(d) the reasons for not acceding to the demands for inclusion of such nomadic tribal castes in the \nlist of STs? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF TRIBAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI ARJUN MUNDA)  \n  \n(a) to (d):       A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n  \n  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nStatement referred to in reply to Part (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *79 for \nanswer on 12.12.2022 regarding “Inclusion of Nomadic Tribes in the List of STs” \n  \n(a) to (d): Ministry of Tribal Affairs is the nodal ministry for specification of a community as \nScheduled Tribes under Article 342 of Constitution of India. The Government of India on \n15.6.1999, further amended on 25.6.2002 and 14.09.2022, has approved the modalities for \ndeciding the claims for inclusion in, exclusion from and other modifications in the Orders \nspecifying lists of Scheduled Tribes. According to these modalities, only those proposals which \nhave been recommended and justified by the State Government/UT Administration concerned, \ncan be processed further. Thereafter, it has to be concurred with by the Registrar General of India \n(RGI) and the National Commission for Scheduled Tribes (NCST) for consideration for \namendment of legislation.  All actions are taken as per these approved modalities. \nIn this regard, a Bill in Lok Sabha for including Narikoravan, Kurivikkaran in the list of STs of \nTamil Nadu has already been introduced in Lok Sabha on 9.12.2022. \nMoreover, the list of Scheduled Tribes is State/UT specific and a community declared as a \nScheduled Tribe in a State need not be so in another State/UT. As regards to demand of \ncommunities for their inclusion in the list of Scheduled Tribes, such demands/ representations \nare forwarded to State Government concerned as recommendation of the State Government is \npre- requisite. \n  \n  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|STARRED   |8", "t": "Helpline for Passengers", "head": "�������������������� �\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n���� ������������������������������������������ �\n��\n���� ������������������