\nUnder the \nFlagship Programme of Namami Gange “ARTH GANGE” \nProgramme,\n \n1.23 \nlakh ha area have been covered along the Ganga basin by developing 6181 clusters. Under \nPKVY 131 FPOs have been formed in 17 States/UTs \nunder the provisions of 10,000 FPOs \nScheme\n.\n \n \n \nIn the year 2019\n-\n2020 the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmer’s Welfare initiated a \ncomponent of natural farming under PKVY, \nBharatiya Prakritik Krishi Paddhati (BPKP)\n. \nTraining \nand capacity building are \nintegral part of the scheme. Under BPKP, financial assistance of Rs \n12200/ha for 3 years is provided for cluster formation, capacity building and continuous \nhandholding, certification and residue analysis while Rs. 2000/ha for 3 years is provided to \nfarmer\n \nas incentives through DBT. Moreover, farmers can also avail assistance @ Rs. 8800/ha \nfor 3 years from PKVY funds for marketing, value addition and publicity of natural farming \nproducts. So far 4.09 lakh ha area has been sanctioned to eight States under BP\nKP.\n \n \n\n \n \n \nA Digital web portal (\nnaturalfarming.dac.gov.in\n) has been launched for promotion of \nnatural farming to display information about implementation framework, resources, \nimplementation progress, farmer’s registration, blog etc.\n \n \n(b) \n&\n \n(c):\n \nBPKP Scheme \nguidelines provide for manpower for handholding and capacity \nbuilding through Champion Farmers & Clusters Coordinator (CCCF), Senior Level Resource \nPersons (SLRP), Community Resource Person (CRP), Lead Resource Person (LRP), Cluster \nOffice Management & Dat\na Entry Operations and capacity building, exposure visits and \ntrainings of field functionaries are as under:\n \n \n(i) \n7 days on\n-\nfield practical training including exposure visit to LRPs and CRPs:\n \nOne per year 7 days training including exposure visit to \nNatural farmers for LRPs & CRPs \nto \nbe provided by BPKP/ZBNF experts and Champion Natural Farmers.\n \n(ii) \nYearly Capacity building of