 \n25 Telangana 5,15,084 14-Nov-18 0 5,15,084   5,15,084 \n26 Tripura 1,39,090 27-Nov-18 0 1,39,090   1,39,090 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 79,80,568 31-Dec-18 12,00,003 91,80,571 334652 0 91,80,571 \n28 Uttarakhand 2,48,751 30-Nov-18 0 2,48,751   2,48,751 \n29 West Bengal 7,32,290 26-Nov-18 0 7,32,290   7,32,290 \nTotal          2,62,84,350      18,85,374       2,81,69,724  11,83,870 4,43,700 2,86,13,424 \n*Electrifi"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |364", "t": "PMEGP in Maharashtra", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 364\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.12.2022\n \n \nPMEGP IN MAHARASHTRA\n \n \n364. \n \n \nSHRI SADASHIV KISAN LOKHANDE:\n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether work is being done in the country under the Prime Minister’s Employment Generation \nProgramme (PMEGP);\n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof, particularly in the Shirdi Pa\nrliamentary Constituency in Maharashtra and \nits status as on date; and \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of Central funds allocated as on date for said programme during the  last three years, \nyear\n-\nwise, along with its utilisation and number of beneficiaries under the prog\nramme, State\n-\nwise?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI BHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA)\n \n \n(a) & (b): \n \nYes, Sir.  \nMinistry of MSME, through Khadi\n \nand Village Industries Commission (KVIC), is \nimplementing Prime Minister’s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) for generating self \nemployment opportunities in the country by setting up micro\n-\nenterprises in non\n-\nfarm sector.  The scheme is \nproviding con\ntinuous and sustainable employment to a large segment of traditional artisans and rural and \nurban unemployed youth so as to arrest migration of rural youth to urban areas.  \nUnder PMEGP, General \nCategory beneficiaries can avail of Margin Money\n \n(MM) subsidy \nof 25% of the project cost in rural areas \nand 15% in urban areas.  Beneficiaries belonging to SC/ST/OBC, Women, Ex\n-\nServicemen, M\ninorities, \nDifferently abled\n, Transgenders, North Eastern Region, Hill and Border areas, etc.,  are treated as Special \nCategory \nand are entitled for higher Margin Money subsidy rate of 35% of the project cost in rural areas and \n25% in urban area\n.\n \nThe maximum cost of project is Rs.50 lakh in the manufacturing sector and Rs.20 lakh in \nthe service sector.\n \n \nSince its inception in 2008\n-\n09 till 30\nth\n \nNovember,\n \n2022, about \n8.32 lakh units have been assisted\n \nwith \nRs. 20,500 Cr. of Margin Money subsidy, generating estimated employment for about 66 lakh persons \nacross the country\n.\n \n \n \nPerformance under PMEGP in Ahmednagar District, Maharashtra, \nincluding Parliamentary \nConstituency of Shirdi, during the last three years and current year is as below:\n \n \nYear\n \nNumber of micro \nenterprises setup\n \nMargin Money \nsubsidy disbursed\n \n \n(Rs. in lakhs)\n \nEstimated Employment \ngenerated\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n237\n \n682.57\n \n1896\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n163\n \n593.64\n \n1304\n \n2021\n-\n22\n \n212\n \n818.84\n \n1696\n \n2022\n-\n23 \n \n(up to 30.11.2022)\n \n84\n \n336.55\n \n672\n \n \n(c):\n \nState wise details of funds allocated, margin money subsidy disbursed, number of units setup \n(beneficiaries) and estimated employment generated under PMEGP scheme during the last three years is \ngiven at \nAnnexure \n–\n \nI.\n \n****\n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI \n-\n \nreferre\nd to in reply to part (c) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 364 for answer \non 08.12.2022\n \nState\n-\nwise position of PMEGP during 2019\n-\n20\n \nS.N\n \nState/UT\n \nMargin Money \nallocated Rs. in \nlakh\n \nMargin Money \nUtilized Rs.in \nlakh#\n \nNumber of \nUnits setup\n \nEstimated \nemployment \ngenerated\n \n1\n \nA & N Islands\n \n28