 NH-139W \n43 \n28 Four Laning with Paved Shoulder of Sahebganj-Areraj \nSection of NH-139W \n38 \n29 Areraj - Bettiah 65 \n30 Ramnagar-Kacchi Dragah 13 \n31 Spur to Smastipur 2 \n32 The highway starting from its junction with NH-139 \nnear \nPatna    (AIIMS)    connecting    Bakarpur,    Manikpur, \nSahebganj, Areraj and terminating at its junction \nwith NH- 727 near Bettiah in the State of Bihar. \n40 \n   Total 1,405 \n  \n  \n  \n\nB – List of Projects completed under Phase-I of Bharatmala Pariyojana \n  \nS. \nNo. \nProject Name Length \n(km) \n1 Delhi Vadodara Package 4 (Haryana Rajasthan \nBorder to Junction with SH 44) \n36.90 \n2 Delhi Vadodara Package 5 (Junction with SH 44 \nto Junction with Keshopura Road) \n36.14 \n3 Vadodara Mumbai Expressway Pkg IV \n(Ankleshwar to Manubar Section) \n13.00 \n4 Delhi Meerut Expressway Pkg IV Km. 27.740 of \nNH-24 - Km 51.975 of NH-58 \n31.77 \n5 Jaipur Ring Road 46.40 \n6 Chandikhole-Bhadrak (Km.62.00 - km.136.5) 75.00 \n7 Ichapuram to Narasannapeta km 470.415 - km \n580.700 9Capacity Augmentation) \n13.45 \n8 Narasannapeta- Ranastalam 54.20 \n9 Chinna Avutapalli (Gannavaram)-Kalparru 27.40 \n10 Chennai-Tada 33.00 \n11 Varanasi Ring Road (Pkg-I) 17.00 \n12 Gorhar to Khairatunda Section of NH-2 from Km. \n320.810 to Km.360.300 (Pkg I) \n40.20 \n13 Khairatunda to Barwa Adda Section of NH 2 \nfrom km. 360.300 to km. 400.132 (Pkg II) \n40.3"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |407", "t": "Elevated Corridor in Puducherry", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 407 \nANSWERED ON 8TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n \nELEVATED CORRIDOR IN PUDUCHERRY \n \n407. SHRI VE. VAITHILINGAM: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the present status of proposed elevated corridor connecting \nMarapalam Junction and Rajiv Gandhi Square in Puducherry; and \n(b) the time by which the work is likely to be started? \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n(a) & (b) There is no proposal for any elevated corridor connecting \nMarapalam Junction and Rajiv Gandhi Square in Puducherry. However, \nDPR Consultant has already been engaged for an elevat ed corridor \nconnecting Indira Gandhi square & Rajiv Gandhi square junctions in \nPuducherry. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |408", "t": "Pending Airports under UDAN Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 408\n(To be answered on the 8th December 2022)\n \nPENDING AIRPORTS UNDER UDAN SCHEME\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \na) whether some airports are still pending under the UDAN Scheme in the\ncountry and if so, the details thereof including reasons for the delay in this\nregard; and\n(b) whether the Government proposes to acquire land for Manduri Airport in\nAzamgarh with the mutual consent of land owner and if so, the details\nthereof?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a): Government has set a target to operationalise 100 additional airports by\n2024. As on 30.11.2022, 70 airports (including 9 heliports & 02 water\naerodromes) have been operationalised across the country under UDAN (Ude\nDesh ka Aam Nagrik) since inception of the UDAN Scheme in 2016.\n \nThe timeline for construction of airports depends upon various factors such as\nland acquisition, mandatory clearances, removal of obstacles, financial closure\netc. by the respective airport developers.The responsibility of implementation\nof airport projects including funding of the projects rests with the concerned\nairport developer including the respective State Government (in case the State\nGovernment is the project proponent).\n \n(b): Azamgarh airport has been awarded for operation of UDAN flights. The\nupgradation work to operationalise UDAN flights at Azamgarh Airport is\ncomplete. Azamgarh airport is owned by the State Government of Uttar\nPradesh, hence, any decision related to expansion of airport, acquisition of\nland etc. falls under the purview of State Government.\n \n*****\n408. SHRIMATI SANGEETA AZAD\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |409", "t": "Construction of Ring Roads", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 409 \nANSWERED ON 8TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n  \nCONSTRUCTION OF RING ROADS \n  \n409.  SHRI NAMA NAGESWARA RAO: \n            SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the details of outer ring roads on National Highways sanctioned by the \n Government across the country, State/UT/city-wise; \n(b) whether the payment towards land acquisition for the purpose is borne \n by the Union Government; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether the Government proposes to construct a ring road in Darbhanga \n (Bihar) in view of rapid expansion of the city and if so, the details \n thereof; and \n(e) the time by which the work thereon is likely to be started? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) to (c) The details of ring roads are Annexed. \n(d)  No Sir.      \n(e)  Does not arise. \n  \n  \n \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO PART (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 409 FOR ANSWER ON 08 -12-2022 ASKED BY SHRI NAMA \nNAGESWARA RAO & SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR  REGARDING ‘CONSTRUCTION \nOF RING ROADS’. \n S. \nNo \nState Name of Project Length \n(in Km) \nWhether the \npayment towards \nland acquisition is \nborne by the Union \nGovernment \n1 Odisha Capital Region Ring Road (CRR\nR) \n111 50:50 basis by State \n/Union Government \nSambalpur Ring Road 34.80 Yes \n  \n  \n  \n2. \n  \n  \nRajasthan \nJaipur Ring Road  (Southern \nCor