 \nGVMCarea(AndhraPradesh)underJNNURM. \n24.29  24.29  24.29  \n6 AndhraPradesh ProvidingIn"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |444", "t": "Installation of Solar Pump Plants", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 444 \nANSWERED ON 08.12.2022 \n \nINSTALLATION OF SOLAR PUMP PLANTS \n+444. SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of solar pump plants installed in the State of Madhya Pradesh under the Pradhan \nMantri Kisan Urja Suraksha Evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM-KUSUM) during the year 2020-21 \nand 2021-22; \n(b) the quantum of funds given to farmers for installation of solar pumps; \n(c) whether the State of Madhya Pradesh has completed the process for selection of \nfarmers/developers for installation of solar plants of 1250 MW capacity on agricultural feeders \nunder ‘C’ component of the PM-KUSUM; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n                                                                   ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) & (b) Under PM -KUSUM Scheme a total of 6514 standalone solar pumps reported installed \nduring 2020-21 and 273 pumps during 2021-22 in the state of Madhya Pradesh for which Central \nFinancial Assistance (CFA) of 30% of the benchmark cost or the price discovered through tender, \nwhichever is lower, has been provided to the farmers. \nThe quantum of funds released as CFA for installation of solar pumps in Madhya Pradesh, so far, \nis Rs. 71.07 Crore. \n(c)&(d) For Feeder Level Solarization under Component-C of PM-KUSUM Scheme, a total of 2.7 \nlakh pumps have been allocated to the State of Madhya Pradesh. Against the allocated capacity, \nthe State has reported identification of feeders for solarisation and conducted three rounds of \nRequest for Proposals (RfP) for selection of farmers/ developers for installation of solar power \nplants and awarded 16 MW solar capacity till 30.11.2022. \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |445", "t": "Development of Road Projects", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  No. 445 \nANSWERED ON 08th DECEMBER, 2022 \n  \nDEVELOPMENT OF ROAD PROJECTS \n  \n445.    SHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA VISWANATH: \n  \n       Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्गमंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government has finalised the Detailed Project Report \n(DPR) of Piduguralla to Vodarevu (NH -167A) and Kondamodu to \nPerecherla (NH-167AG) section; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) whether the Government has evaluated the bids for Nagarjuna \nSagar to Davulapally section of NH -565 and decided to award the \ncontract; \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(e) the  manner in which the Government proposes to utilize its \ninvestment of 88,000 crore to develop road transport in the State of \nAndhra Pradesh? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n  \n(Shri NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n  \n(a) & (b) The section of NH -167A from Piduguralla to NAM Road \nJunction is already 4 -lane. PMC including preparation of DPR \n\nfor  development of NAM Road Junction-Narasaraopet-Chilakaluripet-\nVodarevu section of NH-167A and Kondamodu to Perecherla section \nof NH-167AG has already been commenced and DPR preparation is in \nprogress. \n(c) & (d) The work for development of Nagarjuna Sagar to Davulapally \nsection of NH -565 has already been awarded on 01.02.2022 and \nappointed date was declared on 25.05.2022 and the work  is in \nprogress. \n(e) MoRTH is responsible for development and maintenance of \nNational Highways.   As part of its development plan, MoRTH has \napproved annual plan 2022 -23 with an outlay of Rs 12,000 crore for \ndevelopment of National Highways in the State of Andhra \nPradesh.  NHAI has targeted award of NH projects amounting to Rs \n20,208 crore during 2022 -23 in the State of Andhra Pradesh.   Funds \namounting to Rs 213 crore have been allocated for maintenance of \nNHs during 2022 -23 and Rs 408 crore have been alloca ted for \ndevelopment of State Roads under CRIF in the State of Andhra \nPradesh during 2022-23, out of which Rs. 345 crore have already been \nreleased. \n  \n***** \n  \n  \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |446", "t": "Share of Yamuna River Water", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 446 \nANSWERED ON 08.12.2022 \nSHARE OF YAMUNA RIVER WATER \n446  SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:- \n(a) whether the State of Rajasthan has been demandi ng its share of water from the Yamuna river during the \nlast many years and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether the Union Government has also taken any  concrete action in this regard and if so, the deta ils \nthereof; \n(c) whether the Government proposes to formulate an y efficient action plan to divert excess rain water  i.e. \nflood water of Yamuna river to Haryana border at Na ngal Chaudhary via Taknet and if so, the time by wh ich \nthe said plan is likely to be formulated; \n(d) whether the Union Government proposes to implem ent any concrete plan to divert the water of Yamuna  \nriver to Jawanpura dam, Shahpura, Ramgarh dam, Jamvaramgarh, Jamdai dam, Jalai dam, Amer, Kalakh dam, \nJhotwara, Hingonia dam, Dudu, Nimbark dam, Salemabad as well as Banas and Luni river; and \n(e) if so, the time by which the said plan is likely to be implemented? \nANSWER  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI BISHWESWAR TUDU ) \n \n(a) & (b)  The States of Uttar Pradesh, Haryana, Rajasthan, H imachal Pradesh and NCT of Delhi have signed an \nMoU on 12.05.1994 regarding allocation of surface flow of river Yamuna up to Okhla in Delhi. Share of Rajasthan \nas per said MoU is 1.119 billion cubic meters (BCM) through Okhla barrage and Tajewala Head. Rajasthan’s share \nof Yamuna water from Okhla barrage is released as p er the availability at Okhla barrage through Agra C anal, \nGurgaon Canal and Bharatpur Feeder Canal. \n  \nFor utilizing Rajasthan’s share of water from Tajew ala Head, Rajasthan submitted a revised DPR of “Tra nsfer of \nRajasthan Share of Yamuna Water from Tajewala (Hath nikund) Headworks To Churu And Jhunjhunu Districts of \nRajasthan by Underground Conveyance System and its Utilization” in January, 2021 to Central Water Commission \n(CWC) for technical examination. \n  \nGovernment of Haryana, during October, 2020 and sub sequently in October, 2021, has conveyed observatio ns on \nthe proposal and suggested other alternatives which  the State of Rajasthan has not agreed to.   Chairm an, Upper \nYamuna River Board (UYRB) held a meeting in March, 2022 with Haryana & Rajasthan for building consensus on \nthe issue and a Technical Committee was formed to e xamine the availability of water at Tajewala & Okhl a head \nand feasibility of carrying the share of Rajasthan from various points (Hathnikund, Mawi & Okhla) unde r the \nchairmanship of Member Secretary, UYRB with members  from the States of Haryana, Rajasthan, Uttar Prade sh & \nCWC. \n  \n(c) to (e)  No such proposal has been taken up by the Ministry. \n \n \n******  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |447", "t": "Insurance of Road Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 447 \nANSWERED ON 08TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n  \nINSURANCE OF ROAD PROJECTS \n  \n447. SHRIMATI MANEKA SANJAY GANDHI: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n  \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government proposes to insure road projects in the \ncountry; \n  \n(b) if so, the details of the insurance policy and the implementation \nprocess; \n  \n(c) whether the Government has a mechanism to pay compensation to \nthe victims of hit-and-run cases and if so, the details thereof; and  \n  \n(d) the number of such cases registered during the period from 2015 to \n2020 and the amount of compensation disbursed f or the accident \nvictims in such cases?  \n  \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (b) There is provision for various insurances to be undertaken by \nthe contractor at its own cost in highway development projects. As per \nthe provision of the Agreement, the contractor/concessionaire is \nrequired to maintain following insurance for any loss and damages from \nthe appointed date till the date of issue of the Completion Certificate. \n  \n(i) Insurance of works, plants and machineries \n\n(ii) Insurance of contractor’s equipment and documents \n(iii) Insurance for Contractor’s Defect liability \n(iv) Insurance against injury to persons and damage to property. \n  \n(c) to (d)   Section 161 (as stands amended) vide Motor Vehicle \n(Amendment) Act, 2019, made provisions to enhance compensation in \ncase of hit and run motor accident from Rs. 12,500/ - to Rs 50,000/- for \ngrievous hurt and from Rs. 25,000/ - to Rs. 2,00,000/ - in case of death. \nThe Ministry has notified a new scheme as Compensation to Victims of \nHit & Run Motor Accidents Scheme, 2022, vide notification GSR 163 (E) \ndated 25 th February 2022. The implementation of this Scheme is pan -\nIndia. Ministry has also published rules, vide notification GSR 162 (E) \ndated 25th February 2022, regarding creation, operation and sources of \nthe Motor Vehicle Accident Fund, to be used for providing compensation \nin case of Hit & Run accidents, treatment for accident victims and any \nother purpose, as may be specified by the Central Government. \n             Total number of road accidents occurred under category of hit \nand run in country during the period from 2015 to 2020 is given in table \nbelow. \nType of Collision 2015 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 \nHit and Run 57083 55942 65186 69822 57987 52448 \n  \n  \n****** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |448", "t": "Development of Roads", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 448 \nANSWERED ON 8TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n  \nDEVELOPMENT  OF ROADS \n  \n448.  SHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN: \n  \n  Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n                                                 सड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government proposes to develop Bhagamandala -\n Madikeri-Kushalnagar-Hunsur-Srirangapatna-Mandya route upto \n Bengaluru which will reduce the distance from Pulingome to \n Bhagamandala; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the said proposal is pending with the Government of \n Karnataka; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) the steps being taken by the Government in this regard? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) to (e) The stretch from Bhagamandala to Madikeri is not a National \nHighway. From Madikeri to Kushalnagara  section, the work of DPR \npreparation has been taken up. From Kushalnagara to Mysuru \n(Srirangapatna) section of NH-275, the bids have been invited. In stretch \nfrom Srirangapatna to Bengaluru, the construction work has been taken \nup. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |449", "t": "Upgradation of Small Airstrips", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 449\n(To be answered on the 8th December 2022)\n \nUPGRADATION OF SMALL AIRSTRIPS\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government has any special provision for upgradation of\nsmall air strips and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) the number of small airstrips which have been upgraded in the State of\nMaharashtra;\n(c) whether any proposal has been submitted for upgradation of airstrip in\nOsmanabad and if so, the details thereof;\n(d) whether the Government has taken any decision to upgrade the said\nairstrip; and\n(e) if so, the time by which the airstrip is likely to be fully upgraded?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) & (b): Ministry of Civil Aviation has launched Regional Connectivity\nScheme (RCS) - UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik) on 21-10-2016 to stimulate\nregional air connectivity and making air travel affordable to the masses.\nUDAN is a market driven scheme. An airport which is included in the\nawarded routes of UDAN and requires upgradation/development for\ncommencement of UDAN operations, is developed under 'Revival of unserved\nand underserved airports' scheme.\n \nUnder the revival/upgradation scheme, 6 airports namely Kolhapur, Jalgaon,\nNanded, Nasik, Gondia and Sindhudurg have been operationalized so far, for\noperation of UDAN flights.\n \n(c) to (e): Osmanabad airstrip in Maharashtra is available in the list of\nunserved airports in the UDAN scheme document. However, none of the\nairline bidders have submitted the proposal to operate UDAN flights so far\n449. SHRI OMPRAKASH BHUPALSINH ALIAS\n PAWAN RAJENIMBALKAR\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\nand hence, the airstrip at Osmanabad has not been taken up for revival.\n \n \n \n \n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |45", "t": "National Supercomputing Mission", "head": "������������������� �\n�������������������� �������������������� ���������� �\n��������� �\n���������������������� ����\n����������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������������� �\n�\n������ ����������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����