\n�����\n�����\n��� ���������������� ���������� � ����� � �����\n��� �������������� ������������ � ����� � �����\n��� �� ���������������� ������������� � ����� � �����\n��������������������� ������������� � ������ �����\n������������������ ����������� � ������� �����\n���������������������� ������������ � ����� � �����\n����������������� ����������� � ����� � �����\n������������������� ������������� � ����� � �����\n���������������� �������������� � ����� � �����\n�\n�\n�������������������������������������������\n����\n����\n��������������� ��������������� � ����������\n����� �\n��������\n��������������\n������ ����������� ������������ �������� �����\n�������������������� ������������ �������� �����\n������������������� ������������ �������� �����\n������������������ ������������ �������� �����\n�������������� ������������ �������� �����\n�\n��������\n� �\n\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |450", "t": "ROBs in Darbhanga", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 450 \nANSWERED ON 8TH DECEMBER, 2022 \n \n ROBs IN DARBHANGA \n  \n450. SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR \n  \n         Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n  \n(a) whether the Government proposes to provide funds from Central \nRoad and Infrastructure Fund (CRIF) for construction of five Road Over \nBridges (ROBs) in Darbhanga which faces  problem of heavy traffic jams; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the time by which the said work is likely to be started? \n  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) to (c) Yes, Sir. Four Road Over Bridges in Darbhanga district on state \nroads in the state of Bihar at a cost of R s 219.12 crore have been \napproved by this Ministry under ‘Setu -Bandhan’ sub-scheme of Central \nRoad and Infrastructure Fund (CRIF) in the year 2022 -23. These works \nare likely to be started by the State Government of Bihar in financial \nyear 2023-24. \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |451", "t": "Proposals under Smart Cities Mission", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 451 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 08, 2022 \n \nPROPOSALS UNDER SMART CITIES MISSION \nNO. 451.  SHRI  KHAGEN MURMU : \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether many proposals under the Smart Cities Mission (SCM)  \nwhich are funded partly by the Centre remain incomp lete due to the \nCOVID-19 pandemic that stalled activities for most of 2020; \n \n(b)  if so, the remedial steps taken/being taken by the Government to \ncomplete the pending works; and \n \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a) to (c): Government of India launched Smart Citi es Mission (SCM) on 25 \nJune 2015.  100 Smart Cities have been selected thr ough 4 rounds of \ncompetition from January 2016 to June 2018.  As on 18 November, 2022, \nwork orders have been issued in 7,728 projects wort h around     ₹ 1,81,011 \ncrore; of which 4,963 projects worth ₹ 92,385 crore  have been completed. So \nfar, Government of India has released ₹ 34,087 cror e for 100 Smart Cities, \nout of which ₹ 30,400 crore (89%) has been utilized.   \nThe period of implementation of SCM has also been extended upto June 2023 \nand all Smart Cities are expected to complete their  projects within the \nstipulated time. \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |452", "t": "Construction of Auditorium and Classrooms", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.452 \nANSWERED ON 08.12.2022 \n  \nCONSTRUCTION OF AUDITORIUM AND CLASSROOMS \n  \n    452.     SHRIMATI SAJDA AHMED: \n  \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a)     the details of the schemes approved and executed under Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas \nKaryakaram (PMJVK) in the State of West Bengal, District-wise; \n(b) whether the Government is implementing schemes for renovation/ construction of \nauditorium and additional classrooms under PMJVK and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c)   the details of such schemes pending for sanction/ approval for the State of West \nBengal? \n  \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n(a) and (b) Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas Karyakram (PMJVK), a Centrally Sponsored Scheme \n(CSS), is being implemented by the Ministry of Minority Affairs with the objective to develop \ninfrastructure projects for socio economic development of identified areas. The priority sectors \nunder PMJVK are education, health, skill development, women centric projects, etc. The \ninfrastructure projects taken up under PMJVK are for creation of community assets which also \nincludes auditoriums and additional classrooms, in schools and colleges. The details of projects \napproved in the State of West Bengal, District-wise is given in the annexure. \n(c)   No proposal of the State Governments including West Bengal is pending for approval under \nPMJVK. \n***** \n  \n  \n  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) & (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo.452 asked by Shrimati Sajda Ahmed regarding Construction of Auditorium and \nClassrooms for reply on 08.12.2022  \n  \n  \nDistrict-wise details of Infrastructure Projects/ Units approved to State of West Bengal  \nDistrict Sector Units approved for \nImplementation \nTotal approved Project \nCost  \n(Rs. in lakh) \nAlipurduar Drinking Water Supply projects 31 109.12 \nEducation 96 738.76 \nHealth 8 108.04 \nHousing-IAY 200 150.00 \nOther Community \nInfrastructure 2  142.34 \nSanitation 15 81.00 \nWomen and Child development \noriented projects 58  427.60 \nBirbhum Drinking Water