������������������������������������� �\n������ ���������������������������������������������� �\n����� ���������� ������������������������ �����\n�� �� ���������� �������������������������������� �\n����� ��������� ����������������������������� �\n������ ����������������������������������������������������������� �\n������� ��������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������ �\n��� �� �� ��������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������� ����\n������� �\n�� �� ����������������������������������������������� �\n��� �� ��������������������������������������� ��������������� �\n������ ������������������������������������������������ �\n������� ������������������������������������ �\n����� �"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |470", "t": "Setting up of One Stop Centre", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n  \nLOK SABHA \n UN-STARRED QUESTION NO. 470 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.12.2022 \n  \nSETTING UP OF ONE STOP CENTRE  \n  \n+470.   SHRI SANJAY BHATIA : \n  \n  Will the Minister of WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a)  whether the Government has introduced One -Stop Centre (OSC) scheme under \nNirbhaya Fund in the year 2015; \n(b)  if so, the number of OSCs set up out of approved 733 OSCs; \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to set up 300 more OSCs and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State / UT-wise; \n(d)  whether the Government also proposes to set up an OSC at Panipat in Karnal \nParliamentary constituency in order to extend psychological, legal and med ical \nassistance to the women facing crisis; and \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?  \n  \n  \n ANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n   \n(a) & (b) :  Yes, Sir. As on date, 758 One Stop Centres  (OSCs) have been sanctioned, \nout of which 730 OSCs are functional across the country. \n \n(c) :  Based on encouraging results of the initiative and benefits to women, the \nGovernment has decided to open 300 more OSCs under Mission Shakti , in phased \nmanner, in the districts having higher rate of crime against women or having bigger \ngeographical area, preferably in aspirational districts. \n \n(d) & (e): In the Panipat District of Haryana, one OSC is already functional from the year \n2019.  \n  ***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |471", "t": "PM-ABHIM in Assam", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 471 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 09th December, 2022 \n \nPM-ABHIM in Assam \n \n471 SHRI KRIPANATH MALLAH: \n    \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:  \n(a) the salient features of the Pradhan Mantri Ayushman Bharat Health \nInfrastructure Mission (PM-ABHIM); \n(b) whether the Government has sanctioned any fund under the said Mission in \nAssam so far and if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government has fixed any target under the said Mission and if so, \nthe details thereof; and  \n(d) whether the Government has taken any initiatives to cover each and every corner \nof Assam under the Mission and if so, the details thereof ?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND \nFAMILY WELFARE \n(DR. BHARATI PRAVIN PAWAR) \n \n \n(a) to (d) \nPM-Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission (PM -ABHIM) was launched with \nan outlay of Rs. 64,180 Cr for the period from 2021 -22 to 2025 -26 . The measures \nunder PM-ABHIM focus on developing capacities of health systems across the \ncontinuum of care at all the levels, primary, secondary and tertiary, to prepare health \nsystems in responding effectively to the current and future pandemics/disas ters. The \nscheme is a Centrally Sponsored Scheme with some Central Sector Components.  \n \nCentrally Sponsored Components: \n· Setting up of 730 Integrated Public Health  Labs in all districts across the \nCountry. \n· Establishment of 50 -100 bedded, 602 Critical Care H ospital Blocks in all the \ndistricts with population more than 5 lakhs and referral linkages in other districts.  \n\n· Establishment of 3382 Block Public Health Units at block levels. \n· Infrastructure Support  for 17,788 rural building less Health \nand Wellness Centres. \n· Establishment of 11,024  urban Health and Wellness Centres in all the  States \nwith a focus on slum and slum like areas  \nCentral Sector Components \n· Strengthening of the National Centre for Disease Control (NCDC), 5 New Reg\nional  NCDCs and 20 metropolitan health surveillance units; \n· Operationalisation of 17 new Public Health Units and strengthening of 33 \nexisting Public Health Units at Points of Entry, that is at 32 Airports, 11 Seaports and \n7 land crossings; \n· Setting up of 15 Health Emergenc y Operation  Centres and 2 container \nbased mobile hospitals;  \n· Setting up of a national institution for One Health, 4 New National Institutes \nfor Virology,  \n· Setting up of a Regional Research Platform for WHO South East Asia Region \nand 9 Bio-Safety Level III laboratories  \n· Establishment of 150 bedded Critical Care Hospital Blocks in 12 Central \nInstitutions. \n· Strengthening of the National Centre for Disease Control (NCDC), 5 New Reg\nional NCDCs and 20 metropolitan health surveillance units; \n· Expansion of the Integrated Health Information Portal to all States/UTs to con\nnect all public health labs; \n \nThe administrative approval for Rs 264.00 Crores (FY 2021 -22 )  and Rs 374.37 Crores \n(FY 2022 -23) has been accorded to the State of Assam under PM -ABHIM (CSS \ncomponent). \n \nThe envisaged deliverables under the scheme are, to provide Infrastructure support for \n720 building less Sub Centres, 9 Ayushman Bharat Health and Wellness Centres, 207 \nBlock Public Health Units, 33 District Integrated Public Health Lab and 27 Critical \nCare Blocks in the State of Assam during the scheme period. \n \n***** \n               "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |473", "t": "Women Hostels in West Bengal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT  \n \n LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No.473 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.12.2022 \n  \nWOMEN HOSTELS IN WEST BENGAL \n  \n  \n473:    SHRI DIBYENDU ADHIKARI: \n  \nWill the Minister of WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) Whether the Government has constructed any women hostel in West \nBengal  under the “Working Women Hostel Scheme” during the last three years; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, district-wise; \n(c) the number of working hostel constructed under the Central Government scheme \nand being run by the State Governments, State-wise; and \n(d) the details of proposals under the scheme received from different State \nGovernments during the last three years and the present status thereof? \n \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTRY OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n(a)       No, Sir. The Government has not received any proposal for construction of \nWorking Women Hostel during the last three years from the state of West Bengal.  \n  \n(b)       Does not arise. \n  \n(c)        The details of number of Working Women Hostel sanctioned and functional in \nthe States/UTs is at Annexure-I. \n  \n(d)       The details of proposals of Working Women Hostel received from the State/UTs \nduring the last three years and the present status is at Annexure-II.  \n  \n                                                                   \n  \n  \n*****  \n\nAnnexure I \nAnnexure with regard to reply to Part (c) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.473 \nfor answer on 09.12.2022 regarding Women Hostels in West Bengal asked by Shri \nDibyendu Adhikari, Hon’ble Member of Parliament (LS). \n  \nThe details of number of wo