\n33 MEGHALAYA 18484.66 17693.12 17332.82 \n34 MIZORAM 4814.39 7421.38 5178.09 \n35 NAGALAND 15370.48 14921.34 15465.18 \n36 SIKKIM 2023.9 2429.48 2573.06 \n37 TRIPURA 16615.07 15237.47 18672.47 \nTotal 1681376.37 1579754.27 1820324.71 \n  \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |514", "t": "Procurement of Vaccines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 514 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 9th DECEMBER 2022 \n \n \nPROCUREMENT OF VACCINES \n \n514. SHRI ADHIKARI DEEPAK (DEV):  \n   \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state: \n(a) The details regarding the number of vaccines procured/being procured by the Government \nfrom Zydus Cadila and their cost per vaccine; \n(b) The number of people who have been vaccinated as of today; \n(c) The steps taken/proposed to be taken with regard to the future plan for vaccination; and  \n(d) If so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n(DR. BHARATI PRAVIN PAWAR) \n \n(a) A total of 1.5 lakh vaccine doses have been procured by the Government from Zydus Cadila  \n@ Rs. 375.90/- per dose (including GST).  \n(b) to (d) As on 5 th December 2022, a total of 102.54 crore first doses and a total of 95.09 crore \n2nd doses of Covid -19 vaccine have been administered. A total of 22.29 cro re precaution \ndoses have also been administered. 90% 12+ age population of the country have been \ncovered by both doses of Covid-19 vaccine. \n******* \n \n \n \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |515", "t": "Demands for Setting up of Benches of Courts", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE \nDEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE \n                                                            \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 515 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FRIDAY, THE 09.12.2022 \n \nDemands for Setting up of Benches of Courts \n \n515. SHRI MANNE SRINIVAS REDDY: \nSHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \n   SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU: \n  \nWill the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has any proposal to set up new High Court \nbenches in the country, if so, the details thereof; \n(b)  the details of demands made, requests and proposals received from \nvarious States including Odisha for setting up of bench(es) of various \ncourts in some cities like Supreme Court Bench at Hyderabad, Madras \nHigh Court Bench in Puducherry and new High Court bench in undivided \ndistrict of Koraput and Western Odisha;       \n(c) the present status of the said demands/ proposals, State-wise; \n(d) the details of such demands rejected along with the reasons therefor; and \n(e) the time by which the necessary action is likely to be taken and \nimplemented by the Government?   \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF LAW AND JUSTICE \n \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n  \n(a) to (e):  H igh Court Benches are established in accordance with the    \nrecommendations made by the Jaswant Singh Commission and judgment \npronounced by the Apex Court in W.P.(C) No. 379 of 2000 and after due \nconsideration of a complete proposal from the State Governme nt which has to \nprovide necessary expenditure & infrastructural facilities and the Chief Justice \nof the concerned High Court who is required to look after the day -to-day \nadministration of the High Court. The complete proposal should also have the \nconsent of the Governor of the concerned State. \n\n \n: 2 : \n \nRequests for establishment of High Court Benches in places other than the \nPrincipal Seat of High Courts have been received from various organizations from \ntime to time including State Government of Odisha. The  State Government of \nOdisha has requested for setting up of Orissa High Court Bench in Western and \nSouthern region of Odisha. The Central Government has requested the State \nGovernment of Odisha to work out details of proposed Benches including its \nlocation in consultation with High Court of Orissa. However, no response has been \nreceived yet.  At present, no complete proposal from the State Government of \nOdisha regarding setting up of a Bench of the High Court is pending with the \nGovernment. \n \nArticle 130 of the Constitution of India provides that the Supreme Court \nshall sit in Delhi or in such other place or places as the Chief Justice of India may, \nwith the approval of the President, from time to time, appoint.  \n \nThe Eleventh Law Commission in its 125th Repo rt titled “The Supreme \nCourt - A Fresh Look”, submitted in 1988, reiterated the recommendations made \nby Tenth Law Commission in its 95 th Report for splitting the Supreme Court into \ntwo namely (i) Constitutional Court at Delhi and (ii) Court of appeal or Fe deral \nCourt sitting in North, South, East, West and Central India. The Eighteenth Law \nCommission in its 229th Report had also suggested that a Constitutional Bench be \nset up at Delhi and four Cassation Benches be set up in the Northern region at \nDelhi, Sou thern region at Chennai/Hyderabad, Eastern region at Kolkata and \nWestern region at Mumbai.  \n \nThe matter was referred to the Chief Justice of India, who has informed that \nafter consideration of the matter, the Full Court in its meeting held on 18th \nFebruary, 2010, found no justification for setting up of benches of the Supreme \nCourt outside Delhi.  \n \nIn Writ Petition WP(C) No. 36/2016 on establishment of National Court of \nAppeal, the Supreme Court vide its judgment dated 13.07.2016 deemed it proper to \nrefer t he aforementioned issue to Constitutional Bench for authoritative \npronouncement. The matter is sub-judice in the Supreme Court. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |516", "t": "Opening of Sainik Schools", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 516 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09th December, 2022 \nOPENING OF SAINIK SCHOOLS \n516.  SHRI OMPRAKASH BHUPALSINH ALIAS PAWAN RAJENIMBALKAR: \n         SHRI VINAYAK RAUT: \n         SHRI RAJAN VICHARE: \n         SHRI S. MUNISWAMY:  \n         SHRIMATI DELKAR KALABEN MOHANBHAI: \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE be pleased to state: \n(a)  the number of Sainik/National Military Schools  opened during the last five years, \nState/UT-wise including Maharashtra and funds allocated presently to each school; \n(b)  whether the Government has approved  the  proposal of opening  100  Sainik  schools  in  \ncollaboration with States, Non-Governmental Organizations and private institutions; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the number of  schools opened so far, State/UT -wise \nincluding \n Osmanabad Constituency of Maharashtra and Kolar in Karnataka; \n(d)  the total number of applications received for opening   of Sainik Schools and  number  of  \nthose accepted and r ejected by the Government  / Sainik School Society during the last five \nyears, State/ UT-wise; \n(e) whether Sainik School Authority/Society has  entrusted its assessment report to the \nGovernment, if so, the details thereof and if not, the time by which it is likely to be \nsubmitted; and \n(f)  whether the Government proposes to put the  upper limit with regard to the total number \nof Sainik schools running in a State/UT including Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman & Diu \nand if so, the details thereof? \n \nA  N  S  W  E  R \n \n      MINISTER OF STATE     (SHRI AJAY BHATT) \n      IN THE MINISTRY OF DEFENCE \n \n(a):  No new Rashtriya Military School has been established during last five years. The details \nof Sainik Schools opened in the country during last five years is at Annexure -A. The funds \nallocated to Sainik/Rashtriya Military School s presently i.e. during 2022-23 is at Annexure-B \nand Annexure-C, respectively.   \n…2/- \n\n \n-2- \n(b) to (e):  Yes, Sir. The Government has approved an initiative to open New Sainik Schools \nacross the country in partnership mode with NGOs/Private/State Government Schools in all \nStates/UTs including Maharashtra and Karnataka subject to fulfillment of qualifying \nrequirements and signing of the Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) with the Sainik Schools \nSociety. The total number of applications received for opening of New Sainik Schools till \ndate is 467. Sainik Schools Society/Ministry of Defence, after due process of evaluation and \napproval have signed Memorandum of Agreement  (MoA) with 18 Schools. The details of \nState/UT wise number of New Sainik Schools with whom SSS/M inistry of Defence  have \nsigned MoA is at Annexure -D. No School has been opened in Osmanabad Constituency of \nMaharashtra and Kolar in Karnataka. \n(f):  No, Sir. There is no upper limit. However, Pro -rata allocati on for opening of New \nSainik Schools under this initiative has been made keeping in view balanced and equitable \ndistribution among States/UTs. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE-A REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.516 TO BE ANSWERED ON 09.12.2022 REGARDING \n“OPENING OF SAINIK SCHOOLS”. \nDetails of Sainik Schools opened during last five years on erstwhile pattern. \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \nS. No. Name of School State Year \n1.  Sainik School Chhingchhip Mizoram 2017 \n2.  Sainik School Jhunjhunu Rajasthan 2018 \n3.  Sainik School East Siang Arunachal Pradesh 2018 \n4.  Sainik School Chandrapur Maharashtra 2019 \n5.  Sainik School Jhansi Uttar Pradesh 2019 \n6.  Sainik School Mainpuri Uttar Pradesh 2019 \n7.  Sainik School Amethi  Uttar Pradesh 2020 \n8.  Sainik School Sambalpur  Odisha  2020 \n\nANNEXURE-B REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.516 TO BE ANSWERED ON 09.12.2022 \nREGARDING “OPENING OF SAINIK SCHOOLS”. \n      Details of funds allocated to Sainik Schools during F.Y. 2022-23 \nS. No.  Name of Sainik School  Amount (in Lakhs) \n1 Amarav