ich is a pre-requisite for boarding\na vessel for the purposes of employment\niii. Engaging with Flags with large pool of Vessels for providing Onboard berth for\nthe lndian Seafarers'\nScholarship to women candidates to undergo maritime courses'\nTotal number of lndian seafarers during the last five years is given as under:\nNote: No. o{ seafarers in the year 2O2O &2021were reduced due to the COVID - 19\nPandemic.\n(d)& (e) Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways (MoPSW) has signed an\nMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Ministry of Skill Development and\nEntrepreneurship and Ministry of Rural Development to undertake the skill\ndevelopment and to harness the innate capabilities in Ports & Maritime sector'\nenhance the candidates capacities and skills to deal with the rapidly changing\n,24,478\nZZ (up'to November)\n\n-3-\n, competition and provide for port led prosperity as per the objectives of Sagarmala\nProgramme.\nUnder theDeenDayalUpadhyayaGrameenKaushalyaYojana( DDU-GKY)-\nSagarmala convergence and PradhanMantriKaushalvikasYojana, more than 5,500\npersons have received training for skilling, reskilling and upskilling.\nAdditionally, MoPSW has set up Centre of Excellence in lvlaritime and\nShipbuilding, Vishakhapatnam and Mumbai to augment the supply of skilled\nmanpower. Since inception, institute has trained over 4000 candidates.\nThe potential for ship building/ship repair was identified in Goa. Accordingly,\nrepresentative of such industries in Goa were encouraged by Directorate General of\nShipping to form cluster to be able to pool their resources and obtain benefits under\nthe cluster development scheme of the Ministry of Micro, Small & Medium\nEnterprises (MS[ilE).\nAccordingly, Konkan Maritime Cluster has been setup by the Member of\nMSME at Goa called Konkan lvlaritime Cluster.\n\nAnnexure - A\n1 405025 Dr. B.R. Ambedkar Govt. Polytechnique ANDAMAN &NICOBAR\n2 405051- Vizag, Himt ANDHRA PRADESH\n3 409034 lmu, Vizag CamPus ANDHRA PRADESH\n4 4 140