 Kendriya Vidyalaya-2 in Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh, functioning from \ntheir permanent school buildings , are having  adequate number of classrooms, science \nlabs, computer labs, separate toilet facilities for both girls and boys, assembly ground \nwith stage, canteen, guard room, water supply and sewerage system . Both the KVs are \nwell maintained.      \n \n(d) & (e) KVS has informed that as and when issues / complaints on poor infrastructural \nfacilities in KVs are brought to the notice, immediate action is undertaken by KVS. Panel \nInspection in KV No. 1 and No. 2 in Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh has been completed in \nthe month of October, 2022 and November, 2022 and the team observed that the \nclassroom, cleanliness of washrooms , maintenance of playground and other \ninfrastructure are satisfactory. \n***** \n\n \n \nANNEXURE  \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 777 RAISED BY SHRI KESINENI SRINIVAS, HON’BLE MEMBER OF \nPARLIAMENT TO BE ANSWERED ON 12/12/2022 REGARDING POOR INFRASTRUCTURE \nOF KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS IN ANDHRA PRADESH.  \n \nSTATE/UT- WISE NUMBER OF FUNCTIONAL KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS \n \nS. No Name of State/UT Number of KVs \n1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands  02 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 35 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 19 \n4 Assam 58 \n5 Bihar 49 \n6 Chandigarh  05 \n7 Chattisgarh 36 \n8 Daman & Diu & Dadar & Nagar Haveli  02 \n9 Delhi  46 \n10 Goa 05 \n11 Gujarat 45 \n12 Haryana 35 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 26 \n14 Jammu & Kashmir  35 \n15 Jharkhand 41 \n16 Karnataka 52 \n17 Kerala 38 \n18 Ladakh 03 \n19 Lakshadweep  01 \n20 Madhya Pradesh 112 \n21 Maharashtra 59 \n22 Manipur 09 \n23 Meghalaya 07 \n24 Mizoram 04 \n25 Nagaland 06 \n26 Odisha 66 \n27 Puducherry  04 \n28 Punjab 51 \n29 Rajasthan 77 \n30 Sikkim 02 \n31 Tamil Nadu 45 \n32 Telangana 35 \n33 Tripura 10 \n34 Uttar Pradesh  122 \n35 Uttarakhand 45 \n36 West Bengal 62 \nTOTAL  1249 \n \n  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|10|UNSTARRED |778", "t": "Centra